        "text": "When writing files on Windows, file handles must be closed before calling `os.Rename`. Attempting to rename an open handle results in `ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED`. The writer ensures handles are synced and closed before renaming, with a retry backoff loop for transient file indexer locks."
